{"name":"Dirt Track","hex":"#bb6644","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dirt track","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of unpaved racetrack used for dirt track racing of cars, or similar track racing of dirtbikes.","Synonym of dirt road."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirt_track"}],"entries":[{"title":"Race track","blocks":[{"text":"A race track is a facility built for racing of vehicles, athletes, or animals. A race track also may feature grandstands or concourses. Race tracks are also used in the study of animal locomotion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/BTCC_Brands06_PaddockHill.jpg/330px-BTCC_Brands06_PaddockHill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Race_track","wikidata":"Q1777138"},{"title":"Dirt road","blocks":[{"text":"A dirt road or dirt track is a type of unpaved road not paved with asphalt, concrete, brick, or stone; made from the native material of the land surface through which it passes, known to highway engineers as subgrade material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/DirtRoadCows.jpg/330px-DirtRoadCows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirt_road","wikidata":"Q700143"},{"title":"Dirt","blocks":[{"text":"Dirt  is any matter considered unclean, especially when in contact with a person's clothes, skin, or possessions. In such cases, they are said to become dirty.\nCommon types of dirt include:"},{"items":["Debris: scattered pieces of waste or remains","Dust: a general powder of organic or mineral matter","Filth: foul matter such as excrement","Grime: a black, ingrained dust such as soot","Soil: the mix of clay, sand, and humus which lies on top of bedrock. The term 'soil' may be used to refer to unwanted substances or dirt that are deposited onto surfaces such as clothing."]}],"